# The suite's time budget on CI, judged per split share at the recorded list's
# runner speed: each job and the share total, divided by the share's runner
# factor (the median, over jobs recorded in tests/longest-first with a
# measurable recorded time of at least 2 s, of observed/recorded seconds),
# must stay within per-job-seconds and total-job-seconds. scripts/test.sh
# compares each CI split's times that way, and a breach fails that split
# naming observed time, factor and time at recorded speed; a local run is not
# judged. Set at 1.2× the highest value at recorded speed (rounded up) from
# the twelve retained main ci.yml runs 40834521203 … 41004369454 plus run
# 41000649845 attempt 1 (artifact 12953780855), using this checkout's
# tests/longest-first: largest share total 577.5 job-seconds at recorded
# speed (1.2× → 694), largest single job 52.7 s at recorded speed (1.2× →
# 64). Raising either number is a reviewed edit, not a way to make a slow
# change pass. Check a change against recent trunk CI times with
# `bash scripts/ci-test-times.sh` (tests/time-budget.md).
per-job-seconds=64
total-job-seconds=694
